1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Git tracks your source code. But who tracks what your AI coding agent was thinking?
Every time you switch between Google Antigravity, Command Code, or Cursor, your AI starts completely blind.
It forgets your architectural decisions, hallucinates outdated code, and silently violates your constraints.
We call this Coding Agent Amnesia. And VectorForce solves it.

2
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:49,000
VectorForce is a zero-dependency, local-first engineering memory platform built directly on Node.js and SQLite WAL.
With one command—vf config install all—VectorForce automatically configures all 8 leading AI harnesses:
Google Antigravity, Meta Muse, Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, Cursor, Windsurf, Copilot, and Kiro IDE.

3
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:13,000
When an agent records a checkpoint, VectorForce enforces a strict cryptographic fence:
Unverified model goals and decisions are isolated as Claims,
while real Git commit hashes, dirty states, and SHA-256 document digests are stored as verifiable Evidence.

4
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Launch VectorForce Studio on port 3210 to inspect your system ontology, blast radius, and active architectural decisions.
In our banking swarm demo, five autonomous peer agents collaborate on complex incident resolution without a supervisor bottleneck, continuously auditing workspace drift.

5
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:13,000
With vf reason, Meta Muse and Llama models synthesize your progress, highlighting architectural risks and ranked next steps.
VectorForce gives your agents durable memory with zero runtime dependencies.
Available now on npm: just run npx vectorforce init.
